# Walkthrough - Shared Architecture, White Card Redesign & Build Fix

I have successfully resolved the build error while completing the major architectural refactor and visual redesign. The application is now stable, organized, and features a premium authentication experience.

## 1. Build Error Fixed: Server Component Architecture
I resolved the `Ecmascript file had an error` crash:
- **Root Cause**: [Header.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/shared/Header.tsx) was incorrectly marked as a Client Component while trying to use `next/headers` (via session checks).
- **Solution**: Converted **[Header.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/shared/Header.tsx)** and **[Footer.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/shared/Footer.tsx)** into Server Components. This allowed them to safely handle server-side logic (like session verification) during the build and runtime.

## 2. Shared Components Refactor
Global UI elements are now correctly organized in the `shared` directory:
- **Header & Footer**: Rendered globally to provide consistent navigation and branding.
- **Navbar**: Optimized to show only when the user is authenticated, providing a focused experience for new visitors.

## 3. Premium White Card Redesign
The authentication forms have been elevated to a state-of-the-art design:
- **Perfectly Centered**: Using a flexible, optimized layout for all screen sizes.
- **Premium White Card**: Forms are wrapped in high-contrast white cards with deep shadows and refined typography.
- **Space & Font Optimization**: Improved internal spacing for a more compact and professional look. Added subtle white branding accents above the forms to satisfy the aesthetic requirements.

